From e72865239861c3e57c33078f327edd341c7d442f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 01:31:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 60 fps step 4: battle loops through the helper, battle HUD
 state rolled back

BTL_battleTickFrame (fight, intro, victory and result screens) and
loadBattleDataTick render through modTickStart/modPresent. The render
callbacks that advance battle state keep doing it, but that state is
rolled back around the extra passes (every pass starts from the values the
first one started from, the first pass's results are put back), which
keeps the original order exactly:

- COMBAT_DATA and the fighters' Stats: the HP bars drain hpDamageBuffer
  into currentHP (damageTick) and apply the MP damage; the enemy bars'
  sprites and display timer; the finisher chargeup timer;
- the "BATTLE" start text pieces (only while the text exists), its colour
  timer and BTL_BATTLE_TEXT_FINISHED, which the intro waits on;
- the finisher gauge counters and BTL_FINISHER_READY; the command shout;
- main executable list: the post-battle stat count (STATS_GAINS,
  INITIAL_COMBAT_STATS[0]) and the flee bubbles.

Renders that remove their own object (flee bubble, command shout,
finisher chargeup) use removeObjectAfterRender, so the other passes still
draw the last frame.

---
 src/btl/battle_hud.c    | 16 ++++++++-
 src/btl/battle_main.c   | 80 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/btl/command_shout.c | 10 +++++-
 src/main/btl.c          | 21 +++++------
 src/main/main.c         |  8 ++++-
 5 files changed, 114 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

